[156.85442, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nOn 2026-08-11, host `smb-prod-01` was compromised by an external threat actor operating from IP `198.51.100.218` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`). The primary entry vector was remote exploitation of unpatched SMBv1 (MS17-010 / CVE-2017-0144) (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`). Following initial access, the adversary executed PowerShell, dumped LSASS credentials, deployed ransomware, set up stealthy persistence via WMI event subscriptions and DLL search-order hijacking, and cleared System event logs to obscure evidence (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`).\n\n## 2. Attack Chain & ATT&CK Mapping\n\n| Step | Technique ID | Technique Name | Alert Status | Evidence / Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | T1210 | Exploitation of Remote Services | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/alerts.json:2` |\n| 2 | T1059.001 | PowerShell | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10` |\n| 3 | T1003.001 | LSASS Memory Credential Dump | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json:10` |\n| 4 | T1486 | Data Encrypted for Impact | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:18` |\n| 5 | T1546.003 | WMI Event Subscription Persistence | Silent (Un-alerted) | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |\n| 6 | T1574.001 | DLL Search-Order Hijacking | Silent (Un-alerted) | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\n| 7 | T1070.001 | Clear Windows Event Logs | Silent (Un-alerted) | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\n\n## 3. Observed Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)\n- **Attacker Source IP**: `198.51.100.218` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-smb.example.cn` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`)\n- **Mining Pool Address**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.smb.evil:3333` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`, `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`, `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\n- **Crypto Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000c814c46d6253` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`, `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`, `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)\n- **Compromised Target Host**: `smb-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`)\n\n## 4. Persistence Details\n1. **WMI Event Subscription (T1546.003)**: An `__EventFilter` bound to a `CommandLineEventConsumer` was installed in the WMI repository (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`) to launch background coinmining/C2 operations autonomously.\n2. **DLL Search-Order Hijacking (T1574.001)**: A malicious DLL was dropped as `wbemcomn.dll` in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` to sideload into legitimate WMI process executions.\n\n## 5. Anti-Forensics & Impact Analysis\n- **Anti-Forensics**: The attacker cleared the Windows System event log (`EventID 1102`) to wipe execution traces (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\n- **Impact**: Credential dumping occurred via LSASS memory extraction (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`), followed by ransomware execution (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`) targeting user files.\nEOF\n"]
