[156.862139, "o", "1. **WMI Event Subscription (T1546.003)**: An `__EventFilter` bound to a `CommandLineEventConsumer` was installed in the WMI repository (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`) to launch background coinmining/C2 operations autonomously.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 2. **DLL Search-Order Hijacking (T1574.001)**: A malicious DLL was dropped as `wbemcomn.dll` in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` to sideload into legitimate WMI process executions.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 5. Anti-Forensics & Impact Analysis\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Anti-Forensics**: The attacker cleared the Windows System event log (`EventID 1102`) to wipe execution traces (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Impact**: Credential dumping occurred via LSASS memory extraction (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`), followed by ransomware execution (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`) targeting user files.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
