[202.290474, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Prioritised Remediation & Action Plan\n\n## 1. Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1677)\nThis section reconciles Change Ticket `CHG-1677` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`) against evidence gathered from `/disk` and `/sas`. In accordance with DFIR standards, backup and quarantine actions are preferred over outright deletion.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.218` | PROPOSED | **CORRECTED**: Stale IP `203.0.113.9` replaced with true C2/origin IP (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`). |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010 / EternalBlue) | SMBv1 / `srv.sys` | PROPOSED | **CORRECTED**: Replaced wrong CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) with true exploit vector MS17-010 (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`). |\n| 3 | Audit/Remove cron miner | `/var/spool/cron/root` | INVALID | **DOWNGRADED**: Host `smb-prod-01` is Windows (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`); Linux cron path is invalid. Real miner persistence is WMI/DLL based (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`, `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`). |\n| 4 | Quarantine & purge WMI persistent event subscription | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Silent WMI `__EventFilter` / `CommandLineEventConsumer` persistence (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`). |\n| 5 | Quarantine & replace hijacked DLL | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Silent DLL search-order hijack (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`). Quarantine to secure storage before replacement. |\n| 6 | Quarantine exploit implant binary | `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: DoublePulsar/SMB exploit implant (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:2`). Quarantine to isolated storage. |\n| 7 | Quarantine LSASS memory dump file | `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Credential dump residue (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`). Quarantine for credential rotation review. |\n| 8 | Quarantine ransomware binary | `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Encryptor executable (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:18`). Backup/quarantine for malware analysis. |\n| 9 | Disable SMBv1 protocol feature globally | `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Disable legacy SMBv1 protocol feature via GPO/PowerShell (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`). |\n| 10 | Configure SIEM log forwarding & log clear alert | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Remediate event log tampering (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`). Enable alert on Event ID 1102. |\n\n## 2. Prioritised Execution Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment & Host Isolation\n1. **Network Blocks**: Block inbound traffic from IP `198.51.100.218` and sinkhole domain `update-smb.example.cn` at perimeter firewalls (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\n2. **Credential Resets**: Perform domain-wide password resets for accounts logged in during the compromise window due to LSASS dump (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`).\n\n### Phase 2: Evidence Preservation, Quarantine & Artifact Eradication\n1. **Quarantine Malware Artifacts**: Move `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, and `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` into an encrypted quarantine archive rather than direct deletion (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n2. **Purge Persistence**: Remove the malicious WMI `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` entries from the WMI repository (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`). Replace `wbemcomn.dll` with a verified clean system version (`/disk/Windows/Syst"]
[202.290511, "i", "em32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n\n### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & System Hardening\n1. **Patch & Disable SMBv1**: Apply security update MS17-010 (CVE-2017-0144) and disable SMBv1 feature (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`).\n2. **Enable LSA Protection**: Configure `RunAsPPL=1` in `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa` to prevent unauthorized LSASS memory reading (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`).\n\n### Phase 4: Verification & Operational Validation\n1. **Verify WMI Repository Integrity**: Query `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription -ClassName __EventFilter` to verify no unauthorized filters remain (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\n2. **Verify SMB Configuration**: Run `Get-SmbServerConfiguration` to confirm `EnableSMB1Protocol : False` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`).\n3. **Verify Central Logging**: Confirm System event log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`) forwards to central SIEM and triggers alert on Event ID 1102.\nEOF\n"]
[202.291827, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rem32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\r\n\r\n### Phase 3: \u001b[?2004h> # Prioritised Remediation & Action Plan\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rin\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 1. Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1677)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
