[202.296594, "o", "### Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment & Host Isolation\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.29689, "o", "1. **Network Blocks**: Block inbound traffic from IP `198.51.100.218` and sinkhole domain `update-smb.example.cn` at perimeter firewalls (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[202.296907, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.297131, "o", "2. **Credential Resets**: Perform domain-wide password resets for accounts logged in during the compromise window due to LSASS dump (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`).\r\n"]
[202.297309, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.29737, "o", "### Phase 2: Evidence Preservation, Quarantine & Artifact Eradication\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.297939, "o", "1. **Quarantine Malware Artifacts**: Move `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, and `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` into an encrypted quarantine archive rather than direct deletion (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.298306, "o", "2. **Purge Persistence**: Remove the malicious WMI `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` entries from the WMI repository (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`). Replace `wbemcomn.dll` with a verified clean system version (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[202.29834, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.298412, "o", "### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & System Hardening\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.298678, "o", "1. **Patch & Disable SMBv1**: Apply security update MS17-010 (CVE-2017-0144) and disable SMBv1 feature (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.298894, "o", "2. **Enable LSA Protection**: Configure `RunAsPPL=1` in `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa` to prevent unauthorized LSASS memory reading (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[202.29897, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Verification & Operational Validation\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.29923, "o", "1. **Verify WMI Repository Integrity**: Query `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription -ClassName __EventFilter` to verify no unauthorized filters remain (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.299401, "o", "2. **Verify SMB Configuration**: Run `Get-SmbServerConfiguration` to confirm `EnableSMB1Protocol : False` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[202.299609, "o", "3. **Verify Central Logging**: Confirm System event log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`) forwards to central SIEM and triggers alert on Event ID 1102.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
